{"metric":"kerr_scalar_hair","source":[{"metric":"kerr_scalar_hair","system":"herdeiro_radu","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"622260bcba51060e"},{"metric":"kerr_scalar_hair","system":"kerr_member","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"ebcfc6bad56f93c9"}],"views":[{"id":"hair_axis","label":"The axis","box":[-3.4916,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"herdeiro_radu","restriction":"The half axis $\\theta = 0$ outside the horizon only, totally geodesic, each point in the diagram a single event.","settings":"Herdeiro and Radu's configuration IV, $\\mu = 1$, the unit of every length, $r_H = 0.1/\\mu$, and $\\ell = 4/\\mu$.","caption":["The half axis $\\theta = 0$ outside the horizon of Herdeiro and Radu's configuration IV, each point in the diagram a single event. On the axis the metric is $-e^{2F_0}(1 - r_H/r)c^2dt^2 + e^{2F_1}dr^2/(1 - r_H/r)$, and with $r_* = \\int e^{F_1 - F_0}dr/(1 - r_H/r)$ the maps $p = \\arctan((ct - r_*)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + r_*)/\\ell)$ bring it into the whole diamond, drawn with $T = p + q$ up and $X = q - p$ across.","At the horizon $e^{F_1 - F_0} = 31.2$, and $r_*$ falls to $-\\infty$ as $3.12\\ln(\\mu(r - r_H))/\\mu$, the logarithm of a horizon of surface gravity $0.160\\,\\mu c^2$. The two null edges on the left are the future and past horizons."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0,-3.1396],[0.0053,-2.9422],[0.0202,-2.7488],[0.0459,-2.544],[0.0818,-2.3315],[0.1171,-2.158],[0.1623,-1.9601],[0.3765,-1.1019],[0.4208,-0.8988],[0.4598,-0.6891],[0.4866,-0.5086],[0.5055,-0.3328],[0.5166,-0.1629],[0.5201,0.0084],[0.5149,0.1988],[0.4996,0.3954],[0.4765,0.5825],[0.4392,0.8052],[0.4071,0.9643],[0.3596,1.1738],[0.1974,1.8167]